tools.description:
Calls the tools of the servers by running JavaScript: write an async arrow function, such as async () => { ... }. Find a tool's id and input schema with the search tool first. It runs in a sandbox with no network or file access. What it returns is structuredContent.result, exactly as returned; the text content holds only what it wrote with console.log (cut at about 24000 characters) or the error it threw. Return only what is needed.

In the code, besides everything the search tool offers:
- codemode.call(id: string, args?: object): Promise<any>, runs a tool and resolves to its result (JSON text comes back parsed); a tool that fails throws an Error.
Chain calls, loop and filter in the code, and return only what is needed.

Example:
async () => {
  const branches = await codemode.call("git:github:repos:repos:list_branches", { owner: "octocat", repo: "hello-world" });
  return branches.map((branch) => branch.name);
}
